.TH STRINGS 1 "September 13, 2026"
.SH NAME
strings \- find bounded ASCII runs in files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B strings
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR length ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B strings
utility writes runs of printable ASCII bytes.  The default minimum length is
four.  The accepted
.I length
range is 1 through 255, which bounds the pending-run buffer independently of
input size.
.PP
For an unpacked OMAGIC executable, the default scan covers text and initialized
data and excludes the header and trailing tables.  A packed executable stores
compressed bytes rather than the expanded program image, so the default scan
rejects it.  The
.B \-a
option scans every container byte of any input, including a packed executable;
it does not decompress the image.
